    {
      "id": "3e29f8e2-815a-44a6-958e-1d758e9b1249",
      "name": "Sticky Note",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        1168,
        3824
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 576,
        "height": 880,
        "content": "## Frontline Worker Onboarding Automation\n\n### How it works\n\nThis workflow automates frontline worker onboarding from Telegram, routing incoming messages into registration, document submission, policy acknowledgement, or help paths. It creates or updates Notion onboarding records, uses DeepSeek to extract data from submitted documents, stores uploaded files back in Notion, and sends Telegram confirmations or manager updates. A separate daily schedule checks for onboarding records that are overdue and sends reminders to employees plus alerts to managers.\n\n### Setup steps\n\n- Configure Telegram credentials for both the trigger and message-sending nodes, including the bot token and webhook access in n8n.\n- Connect the Notion credential and ensure the onboarding database has the expected fields such as chat ID, employee name, onboarding date, onboarding status, policy acknowledgement, document status, and any file/page references used by the workflow.\n- Add the DeepSeek API key to the HTTP request node that extracts document data, and verify the model endpoint and request body match your account/API version.\n- Configure Notion API access for the file upload HTTP request nodes, including the Notion version header and bearer token with permission to create uploads and update page blocks.\n- Set manager Telegram chat IDs, employee message templates, shift schedule content, and the daily compliance trigger timezone/time.\n\n### Customization\n\nYou can adjust the Telegram routing rules, document types accepted, DeepSeek extraction prompt, Notion status names, overdue threshold, reminder wording, and shift schedule message to match your onboarding process."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
